A||||8||FieroSoul||Rear wheel bearings||||9||
Z||000000||FieroSoul||10-05-2001||12:53 PM||||  Got a noise in my 84 coming from rear (maybe  right side).  Sounds like a hollow whirring at around 25-30 and again around 40.  Seems to go away on right turns and change pitch on left turns. Whirrrs all the way down on deceleration.  I am thinking right wheel bearing. What do y'all think?||||reg||9
Z||000001||Raydar||10-05-2001||01:22 PM||||Sounds like a bearing to me.<BR> <BR>Just for grins, you might try rotating your tires. If a tire is worn strangely, it could roar, as well. Uneven wear could be caused by bad alignment. My 85 GT chewed up its rear tires because it was misaligned.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||wantav8||10-05-2001||03:20 PM||||My 87 was making the same noise and would also go away on right turns. I replaced the wheel bearing and it fixed it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wantav8.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||terryk||10-05-2001||04:18 PM||||Yep, and when you get it out, it will feel fine. Don't be fooled. Replace it.<P>And don't touch the spindle nut right after you remove it 'lest you enjoy cattle branding.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroSoul||10-09-2001||06:54 AM||||  Follow up post. Definitley the right rear wheel bearing. Not too tuff either.  Had some problems getting that d*%n seal seated right. BTW the old seal failed letting moisture in causing the bearing to fail. Got a lot of good help before I started by doing a PFF search. Thanks guys.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||10-09-2001||10:07 AM||||Seal? What seal?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>Did you take the bearing/hub assembly apart?<P>Did I miss something when I replaced mine?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||10-09-2001||12:30 PM||||There's a seal on the backside of the knuckle where the axle spline enters the bearing. Should be replaced. No fun since the knuckle must come out.<P>The seal is in the knuckle and seals the outer CV.||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||10-09-2001||01:07 PM|||| Awhile back the dealership down here did one of those "shotgun" fixes.  They replaced the whole hub assembly on mine.  250.00 for parts and 250.00 for labor.  I didn't know money grows on trees.????? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||10-09-2001||04:33 PM||||Thanks, Terry. <P>Learn something new every day.||||reg||1
